{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1504","id":4019530073,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO5D6p87vlSlZ","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1504","diff_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1504.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1504.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1504","number":1504,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: run Codex worker visual QA for generated MS screenshots (#1491)","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #1491.\n\nVisual QA gate for the 424 page-level MS screenshots generated in #1490. No screenshot may become a student-display candidate without a `visual_qa_pass` recorded here.\n\n## What was actually inspected\n\nAll 424 screenshots were regenerated locally (byte-identical to #1490 — all 424 image hashes match the manifest) and visually inspected across 24 contact sheets, plus full-resolution review of the 25 pages backing student-display candidate rows.\n\nSheets are grouped by page orientation and letterboxed. CIE mark-scheme content pages are A4 landscape while cover pages are portrait, so a fixed portrait cell would have drawn every landscape page at half linear resolution and made the legibility judgement depend on page shape rather than on the render.\n\nThree evidence layers are kept deliberately apart:\n\n1. **Deterministic pixel pre-checks** — blankness, geometry against each page's own source PDF viewport, hash provenance, colour-overlay geometry. Mechanical; never grants a pass.\n2. **Codex worker visual inspection** of every generated screenshot. The only layer that can see a page is the *wrong* page while still being a perfectly good render.\n3. **Codex worker row/page alignment**, reading printed question labels off each page's Question column.\n\nThe upstream locator (#1489) was produced by a question-label regex over the PDF text layer. Re-reading that text layer here would only re-confirm the evidence that produced the locator under review, so it is deliberately not done. No OCR, no VLM, no external model call at any layer.\n\n## Counts\n\n| Status | Count |\n| --- | --- |\n| `visual_qa_pass` | 407 |\n| `visual_qa_fail` | 6 |\n| `visual_qa_blocked` | 11 |\n| `needs_manual_review` | 0 |\n| **total** | **424** |\n\nRow/page alignment: `row_page_match_pass` 28, `page_correct_but_target_not_visible` 0, `wrong_page` 6, `needs_manual_review` 0.\n\nHard requirements: `student_display_candidate_without_visual_qa_count` = 0, `accepted_crop_without_visual_qa_count` = 0, `student_display_without_row_page_alignment_count` = 0, `visual_qa_reviewer` = `codex_worker`.\n\n## Two defect classes found\n\n**6 assets are clean renders of the wrong page.** The locator aimed question rows at generic front matter — Mathematics-Specific Marking Principles, Mark Scheme Notes, Abbreviations. Those pages carry a numbered `1.`–`6.` list, which the label regex read as question numbers. Affected rows are named with exact IDs in the receipt. Three further rows show the same misfire but already sit at `needs_manual_review` and produced no asset; they are recorded as corroborating evidence without widening this gate.\n\n**11 assets carry a third-party redistribution watermark** — a red band reading `老师微信：liuxue119118（题目有修改过，请加微信确认是否完整，以免影响您的学习！）`: a tutor contact plus an explicit claim that the questions have been modified. The renders are faithful, so these are `visual_qa_blocked` on source provenance rather than `visual_qa_fail` on render quality. The set is re-derived from pixel geometry (a wide, short saturated band pinned near the page foot) and cross-checked against the reviewer's declared list; a mismatch fails the validator. Colour alone is not the signal — 8 further pages carry legitimate coloured Argand-diagram and graph figures and pass.\n\n## Promotion posture\n\n`student_display_allowed` remains false for all 424 assets. This receipt gates promotion; it does not perform it. The 28 `row_page_match_pass` rows are all `exact_located` rows whose locator came from a Layer C source span rather than the label regex, and whose target question label was read off the rendered page.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-visual-qa.v1.json`\n- `post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-visual-qa.validator-result.v1.json`\n- `post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-visual-qa.readback.md`\n- `post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-visual-qa.prechecks.v1.json` (contact-sheet batch IDs + sheet hashes)\n\nContact sheets are binaries and stay in the gitignored controlled package; they regenerate deterministically.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run method-map:build-post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-visual-qa` → `validation_status: pass`, 15/15 checks.\n- `jest scripts/method-map/__tests__/post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-visual-qa.test.js` → 32 passed. Includes negative tests proving the validator **fails** when a promoted candidate lacks `visual_qa_pass`, when a promoted row lacks `row_page_match_pass`, when the declared watermark set drifts from the detector, and when a model call is declared.\n- Upstream `post-attempt-ms-page-screenshot-assets.test.js` → 31 passed; #1490 artifacts regenerate byte-identically and are untouched.\n- Both builders re-run to identical hashes (deterministic).\n- `npm run workflow:codex-preflight` → guards healthy.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-07-09T05:21:18Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T05:26:33Z","closed_at":"2026-07-09T05:26:33Z","merged_at":"2026-07-09T05:26:33Z","merge_commit_sha":"dc0a78fab12bdceeb55a4136e0b274c797c71cb7","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1504/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1504/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1504/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/statuses/096f0e53ec39d002003d8f9c2bf7a151fccb7c66","head":{"label":"Samsen879:feat/issue-1491","ref":"feat/issue-1491","sha":"096f0e53ec39d002003d8f9c2bf7a151fccb7c66","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"ht